{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/pulls/4873","id":3722643667,"node_id":"PR_kwDOLW-eZs7d4wjT","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4873","diff_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4873.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/pull/4873.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4873","number":4873,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"[field] Fix form validation bugs","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is part of the Codex component behavior and test coverage sweep. It fixes Field/Form behavior bugs found during review and adds focused test and adjacent sweep coverage for the affected paths.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Fix Field control name registration and Form values when the name lives on `Field.Control`.\n- Fix stale validation values and stale async validation results.\n- Apply `validationDebounceTime` consistently to field-aware controls.\n- Preserve user `aria-describedby` values when Field adds description or error ids.\n- Keep Field-provided `aria-invalid` authoritative when validation marks a control invalid.\n- Fix controlled `dirty` required validation and `Form.errors` arrays.\n- Reflect `Field.Item disabled` state on the item itself.\n- Add test coverage for the failing and adjacent field-aware control paths.\n\n## Original findings addressed\n\n- [P2] `Field.Control name` is ignored by the Form registry. `Field.Root` documents its `name` as taking precedence over `Field.Control`'s `name`, but registration stores only the root name, so `<Field.Root><Field.Control name=\"email\" /></Field.Root>` is omitted from `onFormSubmit` values and `validate(_, formValues)`.\n- [P2] `actionsRef.validate()` can validate a stale value for custom validators. The imperative action calls `validation.commit(validityData.value)`, but normal typing only updates dirty/filled until a validation commit happens, so custom `validate(value)` can receive `null` or the previous committed value. Existing coverage only checks native `required`.\n- [P2] Async validation has no stale-result guard. Each `commit` awaits `validate` and then unconditionally writes validity state, so a slower validation for an older value can overwrite the newer result. The async test only covers one validation pass.\n- [P2] `validationDebounceTime` only works for `Field.Control`. Field-aware controls such as Select, RadioGroup, Checkbox, NumberField, Combobox, Slider, and Switch call `validation.commit()` directly when validating on change, bypassing the debounce path. Existing debounce coverage uses only `Field.Control`.\n- [P2] User `aria-describedby` props can drop Field-provided description/error IDs. `Field.Control` merges validation props before `elementProps`, and `mergeProps` overwrites plain props, so consumer `aria-describedby` replaces Field's generated IDs instead of concatenating them. Tests only cover the automatic case.\n- [P2] Controlled `dirty` does not affect required-field validation. `dirty={true}` updates public state, but `setDirty` returns before updating `markedDirtyRef`, so `valueMissing` can still be suppressed as if the field were pristine. The dirty prop test only checks style hooks.\n- [P2] `Form.errors` arrays are typed but render as raw adjacent strings. Client validation arrays become a `<ul>`, while `Form errors={{ field: ['a', 'b'] }}` flows directly into `children`; tests only cover string server errors.\n- [P3] `Field.Item disabled` is not reflected in `Field.Item` state or data attributes. It computes item-level disabled and passes it to wrapped controls, but `useRenderElement` receives the unmodified root state, so render props and `data-disabled` are wrong for the item itself.\n","created_at":"2026-05-21T10:09:05Z","updated_at":"2026-05-22T11:17:38Z","closed_at":"2026-05-22T11:17:34Z","merged_at":"2026-05-22T11:17:34Z","merge_commit_sha":"b6ec388df83d3ef3e01bd0505797b63e489480d4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"colmtuite","id":805073,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNTA3Mw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/805073?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite","html_url":"https://github.com/colmtuite","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colmtuite/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"michaldudak","id":4696105,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2OTYxMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4696105?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/michaldudak","